            "body": "Hi @hclsys, thanks for the contribution.\n\nLGTM. The Buildkite logs confirm the root cause. On the regular nightly and daily lanes the Spark GPQA step passes at the default 0.92 (e.g. build 94315: free 114.22/121.69 GiB, metric 0.5657). The \"Full CI run torch nightly\" lane fails on 10-08 (93593) and 10-09 (93820) with `Free memory on device cuda:0 (110.3/121.69 GiB) on startup is less than desired GPU memory utilization (0.92, 111.95 GiB)`. So the 0.92 request (111.95 GiB) sits within about 2 GiB of what the CI node has free in either direction, and 0.6 removes the flake without changing what the eval measures. Two minor notes inline.",
